WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.840
Gorehounds agree: It's a great time to be
a horror fan.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.200
And though 2020 promises its fair share of
dark delights, it'd be a shame if you missed

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.000
any of the macabre horror highlights of 2019.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.540
Prepare to scream.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.880
"Ooh - scary movie…"

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.740
The wide open spaces of the American frontier
are often romanticized by classic westerns,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.320
but The Wind recognizes the terror and existential
dread at the heart of those vast, desolate

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:26.820
lands.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.880
The debut film from director Emma Tammi follows
a tough frontierswoman named Lizzy, played

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.080
by Caitlin Gerard.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:37.860
She's clearly haunted by all the emptiness
that surrounds her - not to mention the ever-present,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:40.060
chilling wind howling across the plains.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.500
Despite reassurances from her husband, Lizzy
becomes increasingly convinced that some sort

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.540
of demonic presence is tormenting her.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:51.900
But is something supernatural really to blame,
or is the root of all her horror simply loneliness?

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.740
It's a question that's bound to haunt anyone
who braves this atmospheric slow burn of a

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.600
horror film.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.020
The Hole in the Ground is a thoroughly unnerving
movie.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.660
In his feature film debut, Irish writer and
director Lee Cronin tells the story of a mother

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:15.480
and son hoping to escape their troubled past
by moving to a remote countryside village.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.320
Needless to say, trouble eventually finds
them there, too.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.540
"Mom look out!"

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:26.760
"It's not your boy!"

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.920
There's something quite disturbing about their
new home… especially that enormous sinkhole

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.240
in the nearby woods.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:36.280
The boy's inevitable encounter with the titular
hole in the ground leaves his mother feeling

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.700
rather uneasy - and rightfully so.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.880
Sure, there's no shortage of horror films
with creepy kids running amok, but Cronin

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.020
handles the material in a way that feels both
modern and fresh.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.460
As The Guardian writes in its glowing review,

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.179
"[The Hole in the Ground] always finds new,
invariably cinematic ways to nudge us towards

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.600
its final leap into the abyss.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.200
Cronin feels like a real find for our especially
insecure moment."

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.060
A horror movie doesn't need to take itself
seriously in order to be great.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.300
Take Crawl, for instance.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.100
This throwback creature feature stars a bunch
of killer alligators chasing a father and

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.260
his daughter after their Florida home is flooded
in a Category 5 hurricane.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:14.560
"Get down!"

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.740
No, it's not a particularly sophisticated
premise - and that's part of what makes the

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.520
film so great.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.819
Critics wholeheartedly agreed, with Slate
writing that

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.379
"It’s fast, efficient, crisply directed,
and delivers on the promised alligator thrills

00:02:31.379 --> 00:02:34.269
[...]. Those B-movie values feel especially
refreshing."

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:39.629
It seems like a straightforward revenge thriller
at first, but The Perfection has all sorts

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:44.019
of tricks up its sleeve… and it takes some
extremely dark turns as it hops wildly from

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.160
genre to genre.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.840
Is it a body horror film?

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.260
A psychological thriller?

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.120
It's both... and a jet-black comedy to boot.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:56.340
The Perfection also happens to be preposterously
gross… and yes, that's a ringing endorsement.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.269
The film involves Charlotte, a former musical
prodigy played by Allison Williams.

00:03:01.269 --> 00:03:05.379
You already suspect she's up to no good when
she seduces the school's current lead cellist

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.620
Elizabeth, played to perfection by Logan Browning.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.840
"Am I the luckiest man in the world?

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.900
I don't even drink and I feel giddy drunk.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.760
My two most perfect students together."

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.550
Before you know it, the film morphs into a
sadistic, gore-smeared spectacular that's

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.100
full of nasty surprises.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.300
Adventurous critics were quick to praise the
film, with Rolling Stone commenting that

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:29.080
"In its own blood-splattered, limb-lopping
way, it may be a particularly perfect thriller

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:29.920
for this moment."

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.580
Ready or Not got a bit lost in the shuffle
when it hit theaters in summer 2019, and that's

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:40.010
really too bad: This well-crafted horror film
is a black comedy and slasher flick rolled

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.300
into one, and it really deserves to be seen.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:46.980
At every turn, Ready or Not manages to be
funny, intelligent, and incredibly well-acted.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:51.780
The premise centers around a young woman named
Grace - played by Samara Weaving.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:56.349
She's forced to play a deadly game of hide-and-seek
upon marrying into a wealthy and highly eccentric

00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:56.840
family.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:01.420
As it turns out, that family evidently signed
a deal with the devil several years back,

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.849
and the pact requires that they sacrifice
a newly-joined member of the clan.

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:09.420
That newly-joined member is, of course, Grace
… but let it suffice to say, she's not going

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.120
without a fight.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:14.660
The majority of critics loved this sly and
subversive film, with Vulture proclaiming,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:19.900
"The movie is a vicious, richly funny, and
artfully brutal tale that places Weaving’s

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.500
performance as its gravitational center."

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.620
Set in the dark underbelly of the Los Angeles
art scene, Bliss follows the exploits of a

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.860
struggling young painter who is clearly at
the very end of her rope.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:34.280
This self-indulgent, self-destructive soul
eagerly engulfs every drug under the sun in

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.980
search of artistic inspiration.

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:40.020
Well, she eventually finds her muse - but
at a considerable cost.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.240
Aided by a seriously vampiric gal-pal, she
quickly spirals into a gruesome and gory nightmare

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.240
of her own making.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.500
The results are thoroughly disgusting… but
is it art?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:50.520
"I don't know.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:51.810
Something came over me.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.389
And it all just started pouring out of me.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:55.580
I don't even remember doing it."

00:04:55.720 --> 00:05:00.320
Bliss is a no-holds-barred assault on the
senses - and in the best possible way.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.880
This film is so visually out there that it's
just begging to become a future cult classic.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:05.880
The A.V.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:06.880
Club aptly writes that

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.680
"[Bliss] approaches its aesthetic with a straight-faced
intensity, pummeling the viewer with [...] violent

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.490
bursts of montage until you feel like maybe
you might have been dosed somehow on your

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:16.490
way into the theater."

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:22.490
In Sweetheart, Kiersey Clemons plays a traumatized
young woman who manages to survive a devastating

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:25.720
shipwreck… only to wind up in another deadly
situation.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.919
After washing ashore on a deserted island,
she's left to her own devices with limited

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.760
resources - and must do whatever she can to
survive.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:37.560
To make matters worse, a mysterious and malevolent
creature seems to be on the loose.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:41.810
With a runtime under 90 minutes, Sweetheart
is a brisk and brutal chiller that dazzled

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:42.990
lots of critics.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.949
Vulture clearly loved the unconventional film,
writing that:

00:05:45.949 --> 00:05:51.400
"[Sweetheart is] an ingenious affair, a no-nonsense
monster movie that uses its limitations effectively

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.260
and tells its story cinematically."

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:58.200
Over the years we've seen more than a few
horror films riffing on Frankenstein … but

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.580
Depraved is really its own undead beast.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.620
If you've ever wanted to see a zombie shamble
his way through New York nightlife, this is

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.830
the film for you.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.260
But you better have a strong stomach.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:12.100
The mad doctor in this case is an ex-army
medic with a severe case of PTSD.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.220
His creation, Adam, is thoughtful and intelligent.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:19.440
It says a lot that this ungodly creature is
probably the most empathetic character in

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:19.960
the film.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:24.940
Rest assured, there's enough gore on display
to satisfy even the most hardcore horror fans,

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:28.560
but the best thing about Depraved is that
it cuts way deeper than your average chiller.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:31.760
"In my dreams I'm someone else."

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:36.240
"I owe you something like a normal life."

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.360
No wonder the critical consensus on Rotten
Tomatoes raves that

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:44.100
"Depraved jolts a familiar monster back to
life with a potent blend of timely themes

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.400
and old-school chills."

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:51.240
Hagazussa: A Heathen's Curse is anything but
a mainstream horror film - but this full-throttle

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.560
creepshow really manages to get under your
skin.

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:58.120
In the 15th century Alps, a young woman has
been deemed a witch by the townsfolk… and

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:00.300
honestly, you might be able to see their point.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.599
She spends her days hopelessly alone, with
only her infant child and her beloved goats

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:05.740
there to keep her company.

00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:09.680
But when the townspeople turn against her
in a violent manner, she descends into a state

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.160
of hopeless madness.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.800
The results are both fascinating and repulsive.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.560
Hagazussa is beautifully shot, without a doubt.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.509
More to the point, it features one of the
most horrific finales in recent memory, so

00:07:20.509 --> 00:07:23.500
if you check it out - and you should - consider
yourself warned.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.500
Neil Jordan's Greta is an outrageous and darkly
campy thriller - but it certainly begins innocently

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:30.020
enough.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.560
Chloë Grace Moretz plays Frances, a recent
transplant to New York City who's struggling

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.120
with the recent death of her mother.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.479
When she discovers a handbag left on the subway,
she goes the extra mile to return it to its

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:44.780
owner: The titular Greta, played with insidious
relish by Isabelle Huppert.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:49.020
Frances becomes fast friends with Greta…
and to say that this French piano teacher

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:51.740
is "eccentric" is the understatement of the
century.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.660
Needless to say, the friendship quickly takes
a turn for the severely sinister.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.640
"People can't keep doing this to me."

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.840
Rest assured, this is certainly not the buddy
film of the decade.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.000
But it is delightfully twisted stuff.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.120
In its positive review, Slate commented that

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.380
"[Neil] Jordan’s deft control of pace and
tone elevates Greta past mere gimmickry, resulting

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:21.440
in a comic thriller whose goofy humor only
compounds its mastery of suspense."

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.540
Set in Mexico and focused squarely on the
country's violent drug wars, the dark fantasy

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.640
Tigers Are Not Afraid is certainly not for
the faint of heart.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.380
At the center of the story is a little girl
named Estrella, whose mother has suddenly

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.620
disappeared with no explanation whatsoever.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.280
In the hopes of calming Estrella after gunshots
are heard outside her school, a teacher gives

00:08:40.289 --> 00:08:44.529
her three pieces of chalk … and tells her
that they can grant her three wishes.

00:08:44.529 --> 00:08:48.840
As Estrella adjusts to her bizarre new life
and falls in with a roving league of fellow

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.720
orphans, she starts to believe those three
wishes might be entirely real.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.640
But make no mistake: This isn't some lofty
exercise in magical realism.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:09:01.480
It's a bleak, unsparing, and totally terrifying
film that critics absolutely adored.

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:04.540
In its effusive review, Consequence of Sound
proclaimed,

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:09.940
"The film is replete with unforgettable images,
stellar performances all up and down the cast,

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:13.360
and genuinely original and thoughtful revisions
of expected tropes."

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:18.740
Little Monsters dares to answer the burning
question that's never far from our minds:

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:22.000
What would happen if a bunch of kindergarteners
found themselves smack dab in the middle of

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.860
a zombie outbreak during a field trip?

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.740
In order to keep her kids from getting scared,
a wholesome schoolteacher - played wonderfully

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:31.680
by Lupita Nyong'o - tries to make the kids
believe it's all just a fun game.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.950
"It is a bit scary."

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.560
"What do we do when we're scared?

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:35.300
What's a song we can sing?"

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:40.060
Meanwhile, Josh Gad plays insufferable kids'
show personality Teddy McGiggle, who soon

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.400
enough falls victim to the outbreak… and
starts looking at children in a whole new

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:43.900
way.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:47.640
Little Monsters proves that a horror film
doesn't have to be deadly serious in order

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.640
to be incredible.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:54.320
It's also been a huge hit with critics, currently
boasting a 93% Fresh rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:59.380
Any child of the '80s or '90s knows Scary
Stories to Tell in the Dark.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:04.300
In this iconic and creepy series, author Alvin
Schwartz gathered up the most eerie and unsettling

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:07.300
short tales from the annals of urban legends
and folklore.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:11.290
The film adaptation brings several of those
stories to the silver screen in a way that

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.680
will be frightening for children and adults
alike.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:21.080
"Some people believe if we repeat stories
often enough, they become real."

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.340
The consensus on Rotten Tomatoes speaks for
itself, claiming that

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:29.070
"[Scary Stories To Tell in the Dark] opens
a creepy gateway into horror for younger genre

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.020
enthusiasts."

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.940
This is a frightening and cleverly constructed
horror film that delivers plenty of jump scares

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.160
without going overboard.

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.140
You've heard of a waking nightmare, right?

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:43.700
Well, Ari Aster's Midsommar plays out more
like a waking daydream, and the results are

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.290
fantastically frightening.

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.660
"What time is it?"

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.779
"9 p.m."

00:10:47.779 --> 00:10:48.850
"That can't be right.

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:49.880
The sky is blue."

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:53.990
The fact that many of the film's horror sequences
unfold in broad daylight certainly doesn't

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:56.440
shield the characters from the dangers at
hand.

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:57.260
Far from it.

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:02.700
This is Aster's followup to his 2018 debut
- the instant classic Hereditary - and it

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.690
involves a young shell-shocked woman named
Dani.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:09.769
She's just endured a horrific family tragedy,
and her aloof boyfriend Christian certainly

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:10.769
isn't helping matters.

00:11:10.769 --> 00:11:13.540
In fact, he clearly wants out of the relationship.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:18.120
Things go from bad to worse when Dani tags
along with Christian and his pompous, pseudo-intellectual

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.410
group of friends, who are heading off to a
remote Swedish village.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.380
The occasion is an ultra-rare, ultra-mysterious
midsummer festival.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:30.320
As we learn more about the eerie pagan rituals
on display, the film lurches towards a druggy,

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.200
deranged conclusion that puts even The Wicker
Man to shame.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.480
This is folk horror at its finest.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:41.980
Jordan Peele's Get Out was an immediate sensation
when it premiered in 2017, and rightly so:

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:46.350
Its blend of unconventional scares and arch
social commentary was a brilliant balancing

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.750
act, and the film is impossible to get out
of your head once you've seen it.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:54.079
Well, Get Out certainly wasn't a fluke, as
anyone who's seen Us can attest.

00:11:54.079 --> 00:11:58.269
The seemingly simple story involves a family
that's being inexplicably tormented by their

00:11:58.269 --> 00:12:02.360
own evil doppelgangers during a summer vacation
in Santa Cruz, California.

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:03.900
"Who are you people?"

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.300
"It's us."

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:11.520
Of course, you should brace yourself for plenty
of twists and turns along the way.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:15.400
The film was widely praised, with The New
Yorker's Nathan Lane writing,

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:20.370
"Us is political filmmaking of the most spirited
sort, and it sets up quite a fight: the Hydes

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.170
come to visit the Jekylls, and the Jekylls
hit back.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:25.420
Whom you cheer for, in the long run, is up
to you."

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:27.960
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:31.680
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
horror movies are coming soon.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.420
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

